{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And if a vow-offering.</b> That he expressed with his lips in his distress." "<b>And a freewill-offering.</b> That his spirit moved him to bring a sacrifice for the Name — not as a vow and not as a thanksgiving." "<b>On the day he offers it.</b> A verb-form from the heavy [pi'el] additional [construction]; and 'on the morrow' means that same day's morrow." "The vav of <b>and what remains of it</b> is like peh-resh-heh in the language of Ishmael, and similarly: 'and he left his servant' (Genesis 24:9), also 'and the earth was desolate and void' (Genesis 1:2)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {3 "'כפ״א רפ״ה' read as 'like peh-resh-heh,' i.e., the Arabic conjunction ﭔ (fa-) serving as a vav; the phrase may be corrupt or abbreviated."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:59.013107125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}